# The lab's front door: one container on 443 terminating TLS for
# *.lab.twolfe.dev and routing by hostname to containers on the shared
# `lab` network.
#
# Routes do NOT live in this file. Each slice contributes a
# <slice>/caddy.caddyfile next to its compose file — a named host matcher
# plus a handle block — picked up by the import glob below from the repo
# mount. Adding a service never edits this slice (the same contract as
# flows/ and the job bridge). See README.md for the snippet shape.

{
	# Every certificate via DNS-01 against Netlify: no inbound 80/443 from
	# the internet, and wildcard-capable. The token is NETLIFY_TOKEN from
	# caddy.env (materialized by the chezmoi bootstrap, origin 1Password).
	acme_dns netlify {env.NETLIFY_TOKEN}
	email trwolfe13@gmail.com
}

# ONE wildcard certificate, not one per service. Per-name certificates are
# logged publicly in Certificate Transparency — every internal hostname
# would be visible to anyone watching crt.sh. The wildcard keeps the
# service list private; the cost is the matcher/handle shape in snippets
# instead of bare site blocks.
*.lab.twolfe.dev {
	import lab/*/caddy.caddyfile

	# Matcher-less handle matches anything the snippets didn't claim.
	# Must stay LAST: handle blocks run in order, first match wins.
	handle {
		respond "no such service" 404
	}
}
